# Slice 7 · NovAI Desk · Atelier Nova Inbox Demo

*PDF authoring (weasyprint) · embedded viewer · public site IA (RO) + About page · download-and-upload-back loop · ~18 authored PDFs across 6 classifier categories · existing 8 docs become dev_source bootstrap*

---

## Why

Slice-5 made Inbox + Ask + Draft real, but the live demo still runs on 8 text-pasted "documents" that were authored as raw strings and have never resembled what a Romanian SME actually receives. To convince a visiting SME owner that NovAI Desk understands their world, the demo must look like their world: PDFs on letterhead, in Romanian, with believable VAT IDs and IBANs, from suppliers and clients with plausible names.

Slice-7 closes that gap for one company. It builds:

- A **PDF authoring pipeline** (weasyprint + Jinja2 templates) seeded by the canonical identities in `ops/companies.synthetic.hybrid`.
- **~18 authored Atelier Nova PDFs** across 6 classifier categories — the public-facing demo corpus.
- An **embedded PDF viewer** in `/app/inbox` document detail so the visitor can see the rendered original alongside the AI's extraction.
- The **public site** at `novaidesk.csmcl.space` — homepage + About + revamped `/demo` — in Romanian, calm tone, no over-claiming.
- An **upload-back loop**: the About page offers a "Try it with our sample company" ZIP download (the 18 Atelier Nova PDFs). The visitor re-uploads to `/app/inbox` and watches the same pipeline they just downloaded from process the same docs live. Demo becomes a closed loop, not a stage set.
- **Public upload boundary**: PDF + ZIP only · caps 5 MB PDF / 10 MB ZIP / 20 PDFs per ZIP · drop text-upload from public UI (keep internal endpoint behind a flag for evals).
- **Needs-review** as a third approval state alongside Approve / Reject.

Slice-7 also reclassifies the 8 existing slice-2/5 mock docs as **`dev_source`** — kept in tree as eval bootstrap + regression fixtures, never surfaced to a visitor. Demo data is now exclusively the 18 authored PDFs.

This is the slice that lets us put `novaidesk.csmcl.space` in front of a real SME owner and not flinch.

---

## Scope

```
IN     PDF authoring pipeline    apps/api/app/services/pdf_renderer.py · weasyprint wrapper
                                   render(template_name, context) → PDF bytes
                                   templates: apps/api/app/pdf_templates/*.html (Jinja2 + CSS) ·
                                              ~5-7 visual templates (invoice · contract · offer ·
                                              email-letter · price-list-row · plain-letter) · share
                                              base.html with letterhead block · use the palette from
                                              rules.constraints (calm dark-gray on white paper)

       demo content definitions  apps/api/scripts/demo_content/atelier_nova/*.yaml
                                   one YAML per doc · references identities from
                                   ops/companies.synthetic.hybrid by short id (e.g., supplier=lumina) ·
                                   includes filename, template, category (classifier label),
                                   meta (date · invoice_no · etc) · Romanian body text

       generator script          apps/api/scripts/generate_demo_pdfs.py
                                   reads YAMLs · renders PDFs into apps/api/var/demo_pdfs/atelier_nova/
                                   (runtime dir · gitignored) · idempotent (overwrite OK) ·
                                   prints summary table: filename → category → bytes

       seed integration          scripts/seed_demo.py · NEW mode: --company atelier-nova
                                   runs generate_demo_pdfs first, then ingests each generated PDF
                                   through the existing upload path (so the real pdfplumber +
                                   analyzer chain processes them — same as a real upload would)
                                   replaces the current 8-text-doc seed for the public /app/inbox

       18 authored PDFs          15 from companies.synthetic cross-reference map (locked):
                                   3 Lumina supplier_invoice · 2 Mobilier supplier_invoice ·
                                   2 PrimaSoft supplier_invoice · 1 Mobilier contract ·
                                   1 PrimaSoft supplier_offer · 1 Dr.Popa client_request ·
                                   1 Dr.Popa client contract · 1 Aurora client_request ·
                                   1 Aurora client_invoice · 2 Bilanț Clar accountant_request
                                   + 3 to round out 6 categories evenly: builder authors
                                   1 additional supplier_offer · 1 additional client_request ·
                                   1 additional accountant_request (identities from companies.synthetic;
                                   if a new counterparty is needed, add it there first)
                                   all in Romanian · all using Ɛ-swap safety in CUI/IBAN/phone

       PDF + ZIP upload backend  apps/api/app/api/uploads.py
                                   POST /api/uploads accepts multipart with content-type
                                   application/pdf OR application/zip
                                   PDF: max 5 MB · parsed via pdfplumber (existing)
                                   ZIP: max 10 MB · extracted in-memory · max 20 PDFs per ZIP ·
                                        each PDF must be ≤ 5 MB · each enqueued as its own Document
                                        with batch_id metadata so the inbox can group them
                                   reject text/plain at this endpoint in production
                                   internal text-upload endpoint moves to /api/_internal/uploads
                                   gated by env flag ENABLE_INTERNAL_TEXT_UPLOAD (default true in dev,
                                   false in production-style envs) · used by evals + seed only

       upload-back ZIP download  apps/api/app/api/demo.py
                                   GET /api/demo/atelier-nova/archive.zip
                                   streams a fresh ZIP of all 18 generated PDFs · cached briefly ·
                                   filename: atelier-nova-archive.zip
                                   public site About + /demo CTA: "Descarcă arhiva demo"
                                   no auth (single-tenant install · public on demo deploy)

       embedded PDF viewer       apps/web/src/lib/components/PdfViewer.svelte
                                   <object data={pdfUrl} type="application/pdf"> with fallback link
                                   for browsers that block inline PDFs
                                   pdfUrl resolves to /api/documents/<id>/pdf
                                   NEW endpoint GET /api/documents/{id}/pdf streams the stored
                                   PDF bytes (added at upload time → app/storage/<doc_id>.pdf)
                                   /app/inbox doc detail: tab or split view "Source PDF" alongside
                                   "AI extraction" · text-only docs (dev_source) hide the tab

       /app/ask source linking   apps/web/src/routes/app/ask/+page.svelte
                                   source pills become clickable · navigate to
                                   /app/inbox?focus=<doc_id> · /app/inbox reads ?focus and opens
                                   that document's detail panel on mount

       needs-review action       apps/api/app/api/documents.py
                                   PATCH /api/documents/{id}/review_state
                                     { state: "approved" | "rejected" | "needs_review", note?: string }
                                   schema: Document.review_state column (default "pending") ·
                                           Document.review_note nullable string ·
                                           AuditEvent recorded on each transition
                                   alembic migration adds the two columns
                                   /app/inbox detail: three buttons (Approve · Mark needs review · Reject)
                                   list view: small badge showing current state · filter chip optional

       site IA + Romanian copy   apps/web/src/routes/+page.svelte                  homepage (RO)
                                 apps/web/src/routes/about/+page.svelte            About (RO) [NEW]
                                 apps/web/src/routes/demo/+page.svelte             /demo refresh (RO)
                                 apps/web/src/routes/+layout.svelte                public nav (RO):
                                                                                    Acasă · Despre · Demo · Aplicație
                                 /app/* stays English (per amended rules.constraints Language section)
                                 copy tone: calm · concrete · no transformation/revolutionary language ·
                                 reference codocz/romanian_sme_ai_companion_promotion_go_to_market_pack.md
                                 §4 (don't-say) and §5 (do-say) ·
                                 hero: "AI care îți cunoaște compania și te ajută să gestionezi
                                       cererile și informațiile care îți intră zilnic în inbox"
                                 About: who built it · for whom · what it does · what it does NOT do
                                       (no autonomous send · no ANAF integration · no fine-tuning) ·
                                       link to companies.synthetic disclosure that demo data is synthetic
                                 Demo: short walk-through of the loop + CTA "Descarcă arhiva demo"
                                       (the upload-back ZIP) + "Deschide aplicația" (→ /app/inbox)

       dev_source reclassification
                                 apps/api/app/models/document.py · add Document.source nullable
                                   enum {"public", "dev_source"} (default "public")
                                 the 8 existing seed docs: mark source="dev_source" if seed runs
                                   in --include-dev-source mode
                                 default public /app/inbox query filters out source="dev_source"
                                 internal "all docs" view (added via ?include_dev=1 query param)
                                   shows them — used by eval + debug
                                 eval harness keeps the 8 docs as regression fixtures regardless

       README + run notes        update CLAUDE.md §Common operations:
                                   - generate demo PDFs: uv run python scripts/generate_demo_pdfs.py
                                   - seed Atelier Nova world: uv run python scripts/seed_demo.py --company atelier-nova
                                   - new endpoints summary
                                 README: short "what slice-7 changed" note (optional · skip if README
                                   is already neglected) · or add to /about page disclosure

OUT    Meridian / Urban Novel Desk corpus     slice-8
       Ask My Company guided experience       slice-9 (suggested questions · archive banner · etc.)
       VPS deployment + HTTPS + nginx         slice-6 (after slice-9)
       Auth · login · multi-tenant            never (single-tenant per install · post-MVP if ever)
       i18n switcher on public site           later if needed · slice-7 ships RO-only public site
       /app/* in Romanian                     deferred · operational UI stays EN until pilot ask
       Real letterhead images / logos         use typographic letterhead in templates · skip raster logos
                                              (avoids fake-brand questions · keeps repo light)
       Send button                            ever
       OCR                                    still deferred · awaits pilot demand
       Auth-gated demo download               public download is intentional — visitor needs it
                                              to complete the upload-back loop without friction
```

