## Constraints inherited

See `ops/rules.constraints.hybrid` (anchored · amended 2026-05-11 for public-site Romanian carve-out). Slice-7 specific reinforcements:

- All identities used in PDFs come from `ops/companies.synthetic.hybrid`. If a new counterparty is needed for the 3 filler docs, add it to that file FIRST (with ONRC check) and reference from there. Do not invent identities inline in YAMLs or templates.
- All synthetic IDs in rendered PDFs preserve the Ɛ-swap (CUI · IBAN · phone · J-number). The Ɛ is a real letter and must render — verify in at least one rendered PDF that it appears as a recognizable open-E glyph, not a tofu box.
- Romanian site copy obeys §Tone (calm · concrete · trustworthy) and §Don't-say from the GTM pack. The English app UI is unchanged.
- Public-site upload restriction (PDF + ZIP only, caps as stated) is load-bearing for the demo's trust story. The internal text endpoint is permitted only behind the env flag for evals/seed.
- No Send button. No auto-send. No autonomous email anything. (Trust principle.)
- No new provider SDKs imported outside `app/services/llm.py` and `app/services/embeddings.py`. PDF rendering is a synchronous in-process operation — weasyprint runs inside the API venv, no external service.
- Prompt hygiene: no new runtime prompts are introduced in slice-7. (Existing prompts are reused as-is.)

