Hard rules (do not violate):
- all identities come from ops/companies.synthetic.hybrid · new counterparties added there FIRST
- Ɛ-swap preserved in all CUI/IBAN/phone/J-number values in rendered PDFs
- public site is Romanian · /app/* is English · do NOT translate /app/* in this slice
- no Send button anywhere · ever · verify in /app/inbox detail and elsewhere
- public upload endpoint rejects text/plain in production (internal endpoint is the only text path)
- 5MB PDF cap · 10MB ZIP cap · 20 PDFs per ZIP cap enforced before any storage
- no raster logos · typographic letterhead only · the demo company doesn't have a real brand and we won't fake one
- no transformation/revolutionary tone in any new copy · re-read aloud before committing

If task 2 (PDF generation) reveals weasyprint headless / font issues:
- prefer system fonts (DejaVu, Noto Sans) that ship in most Linux containers
- if Ɛ doesn't render, fall back to a font that covers Latin Extended-B (DejaVu does) · record the font choice in patchlog
- do NOT switch to a different PDF renderer mid-slice · note as an open edge if weasyprint fights you and degrade gracefully

If the classifier disagrees with a YAML's declared category for more than 2 of 18 docs:
- inspect each disagreement · if the doc is genuinely ambiguous, change the YAML to match the LLM (the LLM is the user's view)
- if the LLM is wrong, leave the YAML as-is and record in patchlog
- do NOT relax the classifier prompt to make fixtures pass (slice-4 hotfix precedent)

Confirm the plan in 3 lines, then start with task 1.
